{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:da188e3b1cefc8a7","name":"Inspector","source":{"id":"source:reference-da188e3b1cefc8a7","title":"Inspector","revision":25832,"timestamp":"2024-12-24T11:40:41Z","sha256":"c42f03ccf4be1b84c4690e9004eb6efae29bca460c4d1e3c71fbd6953b93d4ae","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25832","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Inspector&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-da188e3b1cefc8a7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Every level of government has at least one law enforcement agency, and virtually all private organizations or individuals with sufficient resources have an independent security force on call. Starports and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Stations"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Stations","referenceId":"reference:65763f09c9074f45"},", due to their importance in interstellar commerce, always have a substantial security presence; similarly, all but the smallest private Starships have shipboard security to deter pirates, shipjackers, and mutineers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Inspectors, including customs inspectors and detectives, represent the top tier of law enforcement. Unlike ",{"tag":"a","children":["Security Specialists"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Security_Specialists"}," (who take care of heavy fighting) or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Security Officers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Security_Officers"}," (whose presence provides a deterrent to criminals), an Inspector has to think like a criminal- be it a smuggler, slaver, pirate, or assassin- to uncover their deceptions and find clues to that lead to their capture. In fact, many customs officers have a shady past, taking inspection positions as a way of maintaining a relatively safe and quiet retirement from more dangerous exploits.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although honest customs officers certainly exist (particularly those working in larger starports, with coworkers and supervisors working nearby), it hasn't escaped smugglers' attentions that it's often cheaper to bribe a customs officer than to pay the legitimate tax or fine. Similarly, crime syndicates routinely have at least one Inspector \"on the take,\" often a result of blackmail if not simple greed.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Inspector Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Human"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +16\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, Huttese\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 21 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 19), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},"